+# The Daily Grind
+
+A static homepage using native Web Components. No bundler or runtime dependency is needed. Load `components/daily-grind.js` as a module to register the components.
+
+- `coffee-card`: supply a heading with `slot="heading"`, descriptive content in the default slot, and a native link with `slot="action"`. Give detail links a contextual accessible name, such as `aria-label="View details about Cold Brew"`.
+- `coffee-hero`: supply the page heading with `slot="heading"`, descriptive content in the default slot, and a link with `slot="action"`.
+- `grind-navigation`: supply branding with `slot="brand"` and native navigation links in the default slot. Use `data-outlined` to outline a link. At widths of 700px or less, a native button toggles the links; Escape closes them and restores focus to the button. Links close the menu when activated. Event listeners are cleaned up when the component disconnects.
+- `grind-footer`: supply links with `slot="link"` and copyright or other content in the default slot.
+
+Each component owns its styles in an open shadow root. The page controls section layout and the inherited theme tokens `--primary`, `--secondary`, `--accent`, `--text`, and `--light`. Override `--hero-image` with a CSS `url(...)` to change the hero background. Slotted content stays in the document, preserving native links, headings, and readable content if JavaScript is unavailable.
+
+Run `pnpm install` and `pnpm test` for automated DOM tests covering component upgrades, slot composition, link destinations, navigation state, focus restoration, responsive changes, and lifecycle cleanup. These tests do not launch a browser or server; visual rendering and assistive technology behavior still require separate validation.
